# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `nvidia-*-cu12` versions can change when the environment is rebuilt. Code that depends on an exact CUDA library version might need updates after a new release.\n"
msgstr "Le versioni `nvidia-*-cu12` possono cambiare quando l'ambiente viene ricostruito. Il codice che dipende dalla versione esatta di una libreria CUDA potrebbe richiedere aggiornamenti dopo una nuova release.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Request a package {#request-a-package}"
msgstr "Richiedi un pacchetto {#request-a-package}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If other users would also need a package, [request it on GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). An accepted package is added to the environment in a later release. Until then, or for a private package, [add it as a wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"
msgstr "Se anche altri utenti avessero bisogno di un pacchetto, [richiedilo su GitHub](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-serverless/issues/new?template=pip_dependency_request.yaml). Un pacchetto accettato viene aggiunto all'ambiente in una release successiva. Fino ad allora, o per un pacchetto privato, [aggiungilo come wheel](#add-your-own-packages).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: issue #2017 removes the request template, but the public PR Qiskit/qiskit-serverless#2651 keeps it. Confirm that the link remains. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add your own packages {#add-your-own-packages}"
msgstr "Aggiungi i tuoi pacchetti {#add-your-own-packages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use a package that is not installed, collect its wheel files on your computer, upload them to the workflow's file storage, and install them at the start of the workflow. You upload them again only when they change.\n"
msgstr "Per usare un pacchetto che non è installato, raccogli i suoi file wheel sul tuo computer, caricali nell'archiviazione file del workflow e installali all'inizio del workflow. Li carichi di nuovo solo quando cambiano.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build wheels {#build-wheels}"
msgstr "Crea le wheel {#build-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The job installs wheels without an internet connection, so each wheel must work with Python 3.12 on Linux (x86_64). Collect the wheels in one folder:\n"
msgstr "Il job installa le wheel senza una connessione a Internet, quindi ogni wheel deve funzionare con Python 3.12 su Linux (x86_64). Raccogli le wheel in una cartella:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`Local terminal`**\n"
msgstr "**`Local terminal`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `--platform` and `--python-version`, `pip download` gets wheels for the job's platform, even when you run it on macOS or Windows. It also downloads the package's dependencies, such as `python-dateutil`, `six`, and `tzdata` for `pendulum`. Because the job installs each wheel without its dependencies, upload a wheel for every dependency that the environment lacks, and delete the other wheels from the folder.\n"
msgstr "Con `--platform` e `--python-version`, `pip download` scarica le wheel per la piattaforma del job, anche se lo esegui su macOS o Windows. Scarica anche le dipendenze del pacchetto, come `python-dateutil`, `six` e `tzdata` per `pendulum`. Poiché il job installa ogni wheel senza le sue dipendenze, carica una wheel per ogni dipendenza che manca nell'ambiente ed elimina dalla cartella le altre wheel.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A pure-Python wheel (`py3-none-any.whl`) works on any platform. If a package with compiled code has no Linux x86_64 wheel on PyPI, build one on Linux, for example in a `python:3.12` container. Keep the original file names, because `pip` reads the package name, version, and platform from them.\n"
msgstr "Una wheel in puro Python (`py3-none-any.whl`) funziona su qualsiasi piattaforma. Se un pacchetto con codice compilato non ha una wheel Linux x86_64 su PyPI, creane una su Linux, ad esempio in un container `python:3.12`. Mantieni i nomi dei file originali, perché `pip` ricava da essi il nome del pacchetto, la versione e la piattaforma.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload wheels {#upload-wheels}"
msgstr "Carica le wheel {#upload-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the wheels from your local notebook with `add_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr "Carica le wheel dal tuo notebook locale con `add_wheels()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each path can be a file name or a glob pattern, and `add_wheels()` returns the names of the uploaded wheels. If a pattern matches no files, or matches a file that is not a `.whl` file, `add_wheels()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`.\n"
msgstr "Ogni percorso può essere un nome di file o un pattern glob, e `add_wheels()` restituisce i nomi delle wheel caricate. Se un pattern non corrisponde ad alcun file, o corrisponde a un file che non è un file `.whl`, `add_wheels()` solleva una `QiskitServerlessException`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow before you add wheels, because the wheels are stored with it. They go to a `wheels` folder in the workflow's [file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows), separate from your other files.\n"
msgstr "Carica il workflow prima di aggiungere le wheel, perché le wheel vengono archiviate insieme a esso. Vanno in una cartella `wheels` nell'[archiviazione file](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows) del workflow, separata dagli altri tuoi file.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Replace or remove wheels {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"
msgstr "Sostituisci o rimuovi le wheel {#replace-or-remove-wheels}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To see the wheels that are uploaded to a workflow, call `list_wheels()`. To remove wheels, pass their file names to `remove_wheels()`:\n"
msgstr "Per vedere le wheel caricate in un workflow, chiama `list_wheels()`. Per rimuovere le wheel, passa i loro nomi di file a `remove_wheels()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To upgrade a package, remove the old wheel, and then add the new one. A new version has a different file name, so if you keep the old wheel, `install_uploaded_wheels()` installs both versions.\n"
msgstr "Per aggiornare un pacchetto, rimuovi la vecchia wheel e poi aggiungi quella nuova. Una nuova versione ha un nome di file diverso, quindi se mantieni la vecchia wheel, `install_uploaded_wheels()` installa entrambe le versioni.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Install wheels in your workflow {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"
msgstr "Installa le wheel nel tuo workflow {#install-wheels-in-your-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edit your workflow code to call `install_uploaded_wheels()` before it imports the packages:\n"
msgstr "Modifica il codice del tuo workflow per chiamare `install_uploaded_wheels()` prima che importi i pacchetti:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`install_uploaded_wheels()` installs every wheel in the `wheels` folder. If the workflow has no wheels, the call does nothing. The wheels are installed again in every run, so a large set of wheels adds to the start time of each job.\n"
msgstr "`install_uploaded_wheels()` installa ogni wheel presente nella cartella `wheels`. Se il workflow non ha wheel, la chiamata non fa nulla. Le wheel vengono reinstallate a ogni esecuzione, quindi un grande insieme di wheel aumenta il tempo di avvio di ogni job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: bring only missing packages {#best-practice-bring-only-missing-packages}"
msgstr "Buona pratica: porta solo i pacchetti mancanti {#best-practice-bring-only-missing-packages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, upload wheels only for the packages that the environment lacks. A wheel for an installed package, such as `numpy`, installs a second copy, and the code that imports it can get either copy. Errors from a mismatch appear only when the job runs.\n"
msgstr "Come buona pratica, carica le wheel solo per i pacchetti che mancano nell'ambiente. Una wheel per un pacchetto già installato, come `numpy`, installa una seconda copia, e il codice che lo importa può ottenere l'una o l'altra copia. Gli errori dovuti a una discordanza compaiono solo quando il job viene eseguito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you upload, check your requirements with `dependency_report()` from your local notebook:\n"
msgstr "Prima di caricare, controlla i tuoi requisiti con `dependency_report()` dal tuo notebook locale:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* REVIEW: dependency_report() compares with dependencies_versions() only, so it reports numpy, qiskit, qiskit-ibm-runtime, and qiskit-serverless as \"bring\", although the environment includes them (still true in qiskit-serverless 0.38.0). Fix the report, or keep the note after the list. */}\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The report gives each requirement one of the following statuses:\n"
msgstr "Il report assegna a ogni requisito uno dei seguenti stati:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`baked`: The environment already provides the package. Do not upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr "`baked`: l'ambiente fornisce già il pacchetto. Non caricare una wheel per esso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`bring`: The environment lacks the package. Upload a wheel for it.\n"
msgstr "`bring`: nell'ambiente manca il pacchetto. Carica una wheel per esso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`clash`: The environment provides a different version. Change the version that your code requires, or rebuild your package for the installed version.\n"
msgstr "`clash`: l'ambiente fornisce una versione diversa. Cambia la versione richiesta dal tuo codice, oppure ricostruisci il tuo pacchetto per la versione installata.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The report checks only the supported packages, so it shows `qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless`, and `numpy` as `bring`. The environment includes them, so do not upload wheels for them. The report shows `clash` only for an exact `==` version. It shows a range, such as `>=0.10`, as `baked`. The report does not upload any files.\n"
msgstr "Il report controlla solo i pacchetti supportati, quindi mostra `qiskit`, `qiskit-ibm-runtime`, `qiskit-serverless` e `numpy` come `bring`. L'ambiente li include, quindi non caricare wheel per essi. Il report mostra `clash` solo per una versione esatta con `==`. Mostra un intervallo, come `>=0.10`, come `baked`. Il report non carica alcun file.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot dependencies {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"
msgstr "Risolvi i problemi delle dipendenze {#troubleshoot-dependencies}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `pip install` fails inside the workflow. | The job cannot reach the internet. [Upload a wheel](#add-your-own-packages) instead. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a package that you uploaded. | The workflow imports the package before it calls `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` for a dependency of a package that you uploaded. | Wheels are installed without their dependencies. Upload a wheel for the missing dependency. |\n"
"| The error says that a wheel `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | The wheel is for another operating system or Python version. Get a wheel for Python 3.12 on Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| `install_uploaded_wheels()` fails with `ResolutionImpossible`. | The `wheels` folder has two versions of the same package. Remove the old wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| A CUDA package, such as `cupy`, fails on a GPU compute profile after you upload wheels. | A wheel replaced one of the [CUDA packages](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| An installed package, such as `numpy`, fails after you upload wheels. | A wheel installed a second copy of a package that the environment provides. Remove that wheel with [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problema | Causa |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `pip install` fallisce all'interno del workflow. | Il job non può raggiungere Internet. [Carica invece una wheel](#add-your-own-packages). |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` per un pacchetto che hai caricato. | Il workflow importa il pacchetto prima di chiamare `install_uploaded_wheels()`. |\n"
"| `ModuleNotFoundError` per una dipendenza di un pacchetto che hai caricato. | Le wheel vengono installate senza le loro dipendenze. Carica una wheel per la dipendenza mancante. |\n"
"| L'errore dice che una wheel `is not a supported wheel on this platform`. | La wheel è per un altro sistema operativo o un'altra versione di Python. Ottieni una wheel per Python 3.12 su Linux x86_64. |\n"
"| `install_uploaded_wheels()` fallisce con `ResolutionImpossible`. | La cartella `wheels` contiene due versioni dello stesso pacchetto. Rimuovi la vecchia wheel con [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| Un pacchetto CUDA, come `cupy`, fallisce su un profilo di calcolo GPU dopo aver caricato le wheel. | Una wheel ha sostituito uno dei [pacchetti CUDA](#packages-on-gpu-compute-profiles) forniti dall'ambiente. Rimuovi quella wheel con [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
"| Un pacchetto installato, come `numpy`, fallisce dopo aver caricato le wheel. | Una wheel ha installato una seconda copia di un pacchetto fornito dall'ambiente. Rimuovi quella wheel con [`remove_wheels()`](#replace-or-remove-wheels). |\n"
